 "notes": "Blind pass P1/B. Rotation: P1370687 and P1370700 photographed rotated 90deg (read after rotating clockwise); P1370701 upright, single page (it is the continuation 'entiere...' of a postscript, dated le 4 7bre 1651, signed Louis de Bourbon). Clear text is a rough diplomatic reading only.\nP1370687: archival notes '1651' (top left), '2 E 1841/18 .3', 'M. de Chambon(?)' (bottom left) - not transcribed as text. L14 token '1|none?' is a long slanted stroke with a blob at its foot, followed by a dot, just before 'Vous scaurez': could be a plain 1 or a punctuation virgule. L14/'SYM:sigma?' = small 6/o whose top stroke continues as a long curl ending in a blob (same shape in P1370700 L10 and the renvoi line). SYM:pi (L2, P1370701 L9, P1370700 L11) = low bar on two curled parallel legs (L2 instance has an up-tick/acute-like stroke at right, recorded as part of symbol). 'SYM:pi?' (P1370687 L6, L13, L20; P1370700 L3, L6; P1370701 L8) = a DIFFERENT form: horizontal bar over two legs that cross/converge like an x (could be a separate symbol 'barred x'); kept as pi? for consistency. L6 'SYM:T-renversé?' = vertical stroke with long bottom bar and short top bar (I-like). SYM:K = cursive k throughout. Many diaeresis dots are very faint.\nP1370700: Insertion marks: '+' at right end of L8 (after 73) matches '+' in left margin before '35...76' written at the level of L9 (run L9-marge, placed after L8). At the start of L9, under that marginal text, a few cipher tokens are struck through (illegible, roughly 'xx.4.psi.98'?) - omitted. In L9 after '31|tilde' a cursive word group is struck through (illegible) - omitted. '‡' (double-barred cross) at right end of L9 (after 18) matches '‡' before the cipher line written below 'Cependant' (L14, physically after L13): placed after L9 as run 'L14-renvoi'; alternative: it may be a simple continuation after 'Cependant'. The long curved stroke crossing '20' in that line is the flourish of the subscription 'V', not a deletion. L10 '19|tilde?' digits look retouched (9 may be a corrected 4). L11 'SYM:autre-a+psi-ligature?' = an a-like loop joined to a psi-like sign (possible correction of '44'). L2 '97|tilde?' mark is a short wavy bar (tilde/macron). In the PS (L18-L23) a word group after 'touchant' is struck through (looks partly cipher-like, e.g. '...44 ... psi'), replaced interlinearly by 'Mr L. P. Dafis(?)'. Archival note '2E 1841/18 - 10', 'M. Du Chambon(?)'.\nP1370701: L9 '34|acute 39' written without a separating dot.\nNote: at the very start I briefly wrote three downscaled copies of the photos to /tmp; they were deleted immediately (verified)."
